This package is a port of the `evals` package from pi
(https://github.com/earendil-works/pi), pinned at commit
d6af72e1857cfb10b41d8ff8e69f0d72b4cf6d31.

Provenance: this is a fork-and-adapt port, not a clean-room reimplementation.
The upstream sources were read directly and their structure, naming and
algorithms were carried across; the changes are the adaptations to this
repository's runtime and module layout, each listed below.

Adapted files:
  src/plan.ts                    copied verbatim; no adaptation needed yet
  src/harness.ts                 copied verbatim except two type-level
                                 adaptations: the model-selection environment
                                 parameter gained an index signature (the copied
                                 weak type is rejected by TypeScript as a
                                 default for process.env), and
                                 verifySystemPrompt takes the two option fields
                                 it reads instead of a Pick<> from the unported
                                 harness options type. No behavioural change.
                                 The harness RUNNERS are not ported: they depend
                                 on vitest-evals, which this repository does not
                                 use.

Not ported (present upstream at the pinned commit, absent here):
  src/cli.ts, src/docker.ts
  evals/            all nine — acme-server.ts, configured-runtime.ts,
                    custom-provider.docs.eval.ts, documentation-audit.eval.ts,
                    extensions.docs.eval.ts, models.docs.eval.ts,
                    openai-provider.docs.eval.ts, smoke.eval.ts, tui.docs.eval.ts
  docker/entrypoint.ts
  test/             acme-server.test.ts, configured-runtime.test.ts,
                    report.test.ts
  vitest.evals.config.ts, vitest.test.config.ts

  That is 18 of the 23 upstream .ts files. The eval suites are absent for the same
  reason the harness runners are: the whole eval path stands on vitest-evals, which
  this repository does not use.

  Counted at pi commit d6af72e1, whose harness.ts is byte-identical in length
  to the current upstream HEAD — so this list is a scope statement, not an
  artifact of an upstream revision that has since shrunk.

AMENDED 2026-10-02 — src/report.ts and test/comparison.test.ts were ported after
the statement above was written, so it no longer described the tree. Correcting
it here rather than letting the next reader trust a stale provenance list:

  src/report.ts            copied byte-identical except the `@vitest-evals/core`
                           seam described in its own header. That package is
                           npm-only and is absent from pi-ref's node_modules as
                           well, so it is not a gap `bun install` closes. Only
                           `persistSession` needs it; the comparison contract
                           never reaches that function, so the import is deferred
                           rather than replaced and the pure half stays verbatim.
  test/comparison.test.ts  copied byte-identical except `vitest` -> `bun:test`.

  The amended claim is narrower than "report.ts is portable": its comparison
  half is. `persistSession` still throws, deliberately and by name, and the eval
  suites that would exercise it remain unported. The earlier reasoning that
  report.ts "is not independently portable either" was true of the whole file and
  wrong about the half — a file can be split by which function a contract reaches.

  Verified by mutation, not by green: swapping the `lift` arguments fails the
  paired-delta test, and making `eligiblePairs` ignore blocked filtering fails all
  four. Both restored from a copy with `git diff` empty. Suite is 28 tests across
  3 files, up from 24.

